Description: Matplotlib's 3D plots in stereo
 A module for Matplotlib (stereo_matplotlib) that shows a figure's 3D axes
 to each eye from its own camera: two parallel cameras whose offset is fitted
 so that every point of the figure stays inside the depth the person set for
 the desktop. An interactive figure in a Tk or Qt window on X11 shows its 3D
 area as a pair on Sparky Stereo OS's desktop, with Enable 3D and the 3D
 display settings in its toolbar; stills are written as PNG with the stereo
 mark (sTER, .pns) or JPEG with the JPS block, animations as marked
 side-by-side frames or video.
